    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d913">

                <pb facs="0917" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/6619</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (Page) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2745]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 13, 1916</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous
                        correspondence<anchor n="2" xml:id="d913-f1"/> in regard to the steamship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Esrom</hi> and to various items of her cargo which
                    the British authorities have ordered to be placed in the prize court, I now have
                    the honor to enclose herewith for the information of the Department <pb
                        facs="0918" n="660" xml:id="pg660"/> a copy of a note addressed to the
                    Foreign Office by the Embassy on December 13 in this regard together with a copy
                    of the reply received from the Foreign Office under date of the 25th instant, in
                    which the attitude of the British Government in reference to the cargo of this
                    vessel is set forth.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Hines Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d913-a1.xml" xpointer="d913-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d913-a2.xml" xpointer="d913-a2"/>
            </div>
